    "updated_at": "2017-11-07T12:38:50Z",
    "body": "I tried to think through the security argument. It seems that if you only have `text/javascript;goal=module` scripts and you enforce that through a MIME type you can be positive they can only be executed on the same origin (or origins you opted into with CORS) the moment all clients relevant to you have implemented this change.\r\n\r\nAnother thing to test:\r\n\r\n* Goal parameter specified on a non-JavaScript MIME type.",
